# Corpus unit bbox/C05 — gap (generalization; cross_model_transfer_evaluation -> controlled_comparison)
#
# Source: bbox C05 annotation (generalization, double-annotated; corpus pin 62e9b54).
# Headline: the frozen BBOX-ADAPTER (trained on gpt-3.5-turbo) plugs into davinci-002 (+6.85 avg
# over 3 datasets) and Mixtral-8x7B (+4.50) with no retraining.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: cross_model_transfer_evaluation -> controlled_comparison. The binding comparison
#     is adapted vs unadapted on the tested targets; S = bbox_adapter, B = unadapted_target,
#     Q = transfer_accuracy, D = new_black_box_llms (the two named targets). The open-class
#     quantifier "other black-box LLMs" (annotation coverage_flag) is not expressible in flat
#     pred(args) vocabulary — recorded here; the atom encodes only the tested instances.
#   * The annotation's mandatory CQ3 is unmet-gap: the adapted arm draws extra beam-search samples
#     (k=3) with no sampling-matched control, so the +6.85/+4.50 gains are not validly attributable
#     to the transferred adapter alone. Mapped onto policy-mandatory measurement_validity -> unmet.
#     The incomplete controlled_comparison argument is declared as a located hole with
#     `open measurement_validity` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under `lara-core@0.3`): it is
#     not an AF node, so the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * CQ1 (no retraining) and CQ2 (same prompts/test sets per target) discharge baseline_parity;
#     that leaf is on the page. The optional scope-adequacy CQ4 is unmet, so the optional
#     scope_match is opened (R5 accounting; no obligation).
#   * variance_reported also has no leaf (only per-target averages, no per-dataset cells or repeats)
#     — a second policy-mandatory blocker, also opened; measurement_validity is the
#     annotation-grounded driver.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact bbox at sha256:bb06e592cef6
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c05
  nl      = "The frozen BBOX-ADAPTER trained on gpt-3.5-turbo plugs into davinci-002 (+6.85 avg over 3 datasets) and Mixtral-8x7B (+4.50) with no retraining; per-dataset cells and a sampling-matched control are absent"
  formal  = better(bbox_adapter, unadapted_target, transfer_accuracy, new_black_box_llms)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e02, compares(bbox_adapter, unadapted_target, transfer_accuracy, new_black_box_llms, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C05, logic/experiments.md#E02]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(bbox_adapter, unadapted_target, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-steps-1-5]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is declared as a located hole ------------------------------

# valid_measurement(transfer_accuracy, e02) has no honest leaf (the adapted arm's extra
# beam-search samples are never controlled, CQ3) and variance_reported(e02) has none either
# (per-target averages only). Both are policy-mandatory and stay open: a1 is a hole, not an AF
# node. scope_match (optional, CQ4 unmet) is opened as well.
arg a1 : supports(c05) by controlled_comparison(bbox_adapter, unadapted_target, transfer_accuracy, new_black_box_llms, e02)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  open      measurement_validity
  open      variance_reported
  open      scope_match

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments.
# Located hole: a1 (open obligations [measurement_validity, variance_reported]; sources no attacks).
# Claim status:
#   c05 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8 — the hole
#               is reported, not a node)
